cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Wenn du R9-SI zitierst, dann so · If you cite R9-SI, please cite it like this."
title: "R9-SI: a whole voxel world in one HTML file"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: n0t3
    website: "https://github.com/n0t3-droid"
repository-code: "https://github.com/n0t3-droid/R9-SI"
url: "https://n0t3-droid.github.io/R9-SI/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An open-source browser voxel game and editor (WebGL 2, web workers, no engine, no dependencies) built entirely from
  its own procedural code: fractal simplex terrain with versioned, byte-identical generation; light flood fill; surface
  nets; horizon culling with a proof test; Rayleigh/Mie skies, GGX materials and an ACES tone curve; Karplus–Strong
  strings and Eyring reverberation; Kepler orbits coasted with universal variables; and a quality governor that
  forecasts the frame cost. Every formula is documented with the file it lives in.
keywords:
  - voxel
  - webgl2
  - procedural generation
  - simplex noise
  - horizon culling
  - physically based rendering
  - karplus-strong
  - room acoustics
  - orbital mechanics
  - browser game
